  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A metal exposed to light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and emits photoelectrons with a certain kinetic energy. The maximum kinetic energy of photo-electron doubles when light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> is used. The work function of the metal is</p><p>(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1230</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>).</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>537</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>615</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According to Einstein&#39;s photoelectric equation</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1230</mn><mn>800</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1230</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1230</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Eliminating <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> from (1) and (2) we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1230</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1230</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>615</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
